On Tue, Sep 8, 2009 at 9:01 AM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:

> mi'u mi ai mi'e tijlan
>
> A suggestion: how about having a taboo word or two that should not be
> formed in a certain subtle way? "bongu", for example:
>
> i *b*a lo nu citka kei le gerku cu *dansu*
> i *o*i ko na *sutra *lo ka carna
> i *n*e'a lo palta le gerku za'o *traji *lo ka carna
> i *g*e po'o nai mi gi ji'a ko *jinme*
> i *u*'u bai do mi co'u *melbi*
>
> The utterer of the last sentence beginning with "u" (ignoring "i") gets
> eliminated.
>
> This could be a strategic trap into which one is led by other players
> working together to furtively prepare "bong-". But falling into that
> wouldn't be very likely, for there aren't many jbovla beginning with "u" and
> it would be extremely hard to trick a player into actually using one of such
> words at that specific place in the sentence.
>

